{"parentUuid":"9e8cf52c-18b5-4f7b-8a31-b7f766824604","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01SEJKXxWXNJb2dmnrXqme4p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EpWTvuCHp3d55sW2WacqEr","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"allowedPrompts":[{"tool":"Bash","prompt":"run mise check / go test in versioncheck package"}],"plan":"# Align auto-update prompt across all installers\n\n## Context\n\nPR #1057 (commit `ab7a8151b`) added a 3-option auto-update prompt for the **brew** installer:\n\n```\nUpdate available! 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0\nRelease notes: https://github.com/entireio/cli/releases/tag/v2.0.0\n1. Update now (runs `brew upgrade entire`)\n2. Skip\n3. Skip until next version\n```\n\nPicking option 3 persists the version in `~/.config/entire/version_check.json` so the user is not re-prompted until a newer release ships.\n\nOther installers (mise, scoop, curl-bash) still show the older single-question huh form (`\"Install the new version now?\" Yes/No`) with no skip-until-next-version option. The user wants the new 3-option flow used for **every** installer that supports auto-installation.\n\nOutcome: a single prompt UX across brew/mise/scoop/curl-bash. Skip-until-next-version available everywhere. No duplicate code paths.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Generalize the existing brew flow.** The brew prompt is already installer-agnostic in everything but its name — the message uses `cmdStr := updateCommand(currentVersion)`, the choice parser doesn't care about brew, and the cache persistence in `CheckAndNotify` already handles `autoUpdateActionSkipUntilNextVersion` regardless of installer. The change is mostly mechanical: drop the brew-only branch, rename, delete the dead Y/N path.\n\nConcrete changes:\n\n1. **`cmd/entire/cli/versioncheck/autoupdate.go`**\n   - Delete the brew-only dispatch in `MaybeAutoUpdate` (lines 53–55) and inline the brew flow as the single path for all installers where `canAutoInstall()` is true.\n   - Preserve the existing **Windows + unknown installer** branch (lines 62–65): when we cannot auto-install, print the \"download from <downloadsURL>\" message and return `autoUpdateActionSkip` (unchanged). No prompt — there is no command to run, so the 3-option prompt has nothing to offer.\n   - Rename to drop the \"Brew\" prefix:\n     - `maybeBrewAutoUpdate` → fold into `MaybeAutoUpdate` (no separate function needed once it's the only path)\n     - `printBrewUpdateMessage` → `printUpdateMessage`\n     - `chooseBrewUpdate` (test seam) → `chooseUpdate`\n     - `realChooseBrewUpdate` → `realChooseUpdate`\n     - `chooseBrewUpdateFromReader` → `chooseUpdateFromReader`\n     - `parseBrewUpdateChoice` → `parseUpdateChoice`\n   - **Delete** the now-unused Y/N huh form: `realConfirmUpdate` (lines 170–192) and the `confirmUpdate` test seam (line 35). The 3-option flow replaces it for every installer; the huh form has no remaining caller.\n\n2. **`cmd/entire/cli/versioncheck/autoupdate_test.go`**\n   - Rename existing brew-named tests/helpers to drop \"Brew\" where they exercise the now-generic path.\n   - Drop tests of the deleted `confirmUpdate` huh form.\n   - Add table-driven coverage for each installer (`installManagerMise`, `installManagerScoop`, `installManagerUnknown` on non-Windows): same 3 options, same parser, but the `cmdStr` shown in option 1 differs per `updateCommand()`. Mirror the existing brew tests:\n     - Option 1 (or empty) → `runInstaller` invoked with the right command, returns `autoUpdateActionUpdate`\n     - Option 2 → returns `autoUpdateActionSkip`, installer not invoked\n     - Option 3 → returns `autoUpdateActionSkipUntilNextVersion`, installer not invoked\n     - Kill switch / non-interactive / non-TTY → prints \"To update, run: <cmd>\" hint, returns skip\n   - Add a regression test that `installManagerUnknown` on **Windows** still hits the downloads-URL path and does not prompt.\n\n3. **`cmd/entire/cli/versioncheck/versioncheck_test.go`**\n   - The `SkippedVersion` cache test already exists for brew (`TestCheckAndNotify_SavesSkippedVersionOnSkipUntilNextVersion`). Extend with a mise/scoop case to lock in that the cache is installer-agnostic. This is cheap and proves the persistence path works for the new installers without code changes.\n\nNo changes needed in:\n- `versioncheck.go` — the `CheckAndNotify` skip-version persistence (lines 89–96) is already installer-agnostic.\n- `types.go` — `VersionCache.SkippedVersion` already exists.\n- `updateCommand()` / `installManagerForCurrentBinary()` / `canAutoInstall()` — already correct.\n- Settings, scripts, install paths — out of scope; this is a runtime UX change only.\n\n## Critical files\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/versioncheck/autoupdate.go` — main change (collapse brew branch, rename, delete dead Y/N form)\n- `cmd/entire/cli/versioncheck/autoupdate_test.go` — rename + add per-installer tests\n- `cmd/entire/cli/versioncheck/versioncheck_test.go` — add a non-brew skip-persistence test\n\n## Reusable existing helpers\n\n- `updateCommand(currentVersion)` in `versioncheck.go:396` — already returns the correct shell command per installer/channel; the prompt's option 1 reads from this.\n- `installManagerForCurrentBinary()` in `versioncheck.go:348` — installer detection.\n- `canAutoInstall()` in `versioncheck.go:379` — gates the Windows+unknown fallback.\n- `printNotification()` in `versioncheck.go:416` — header used in the non-interactive fallback path.\n- `interactive.CanPromptInteractively()` and `isTerminalOut(w)` — interactivity gate, already wired.\n- `useBrewExecutable()` test helper in `autoupdate_test.go:55` — generalize or add `useMiseExecutable`/`useScoopExecutable`/`useUnknownExecutable` siblings using the same pattern.\n- `autoUpdateFixture` in `autoupdate_test.go:13` — already mocks `runInstaller`, `chooseBrewUpdate`, `isTerminalOut`; reuse for the new tests after renaming the seam.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `mise run check` — formats, lints, runs unit + integration tests + Vogon canary.\n2. Targeted unit tests: `mise run test -- ./cmd/entire/cli/versioncheck/...` (or `go test`) — confirms all renamed/added tests pass.\n3. Manual smoke (optional, against a real release tag mismatch):\n   - Build `entire` from this branch and place the binary under a path matching each detector pattern (e.g., `tmp/mise/installs/entire/x.y.z/entire`, `tmp/scoop/apps/entire/x.y.z/entire.exe`, plain `~/.local/bin/entire`).\n   - Force the version-check cache to think a new version exists (`echo '{}' > ~/.config/entire/version_check.json`) and run any command — verify the 3-option prompt appears with the correct `runs <cmdStr>` text per installer.\n   - Pick option 3, re-run, verify no re-prompt; bump the cached `SkippedVersion` to a stale value, verify the prompt returns.\n4. `ENTIRE_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1 entire <cmd>` — confirms the kill switch still suppresses the prompt and prints the manual hint for every installer.\n5. CI on the branch — relies on `mise run check` passing; no special CI steps needed.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Adding a \"skip until next version\" option for the Windows+unknown installer (no command to run; current \"download from URL\" behavior stays).\n- Any change to install scripts (`scripts/install.sh`), settings schema, or the `entire status` / `entire version` command surface.\n- Background / async update checks, new `entire update` command, or notification frequency changes.\n","planFilePath":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/.claude/plans/i-did-see-this-curious-cosmos.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3160,"cache_read_input_tokens":97663,"output_tokens":124,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3160,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":124,"cache_read_input_to